    "created_at": "2015-11-04T16:19:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-04T16:19:27Z",
    "body": "To clarify, if an \"outer fetch()\" is intercepted by a SW which then makes an \"inner fetch()\":\n\n1) Clearly the outer fetch() should be canceled when the window is closed/stopped\n2) But should the inner fetch() be part of that same fetch group and canceled?\n3) It seems (2) is only possible if the inner fetch() uses event.request\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
